diff --git a/HISTORY.md b/HISTORY.md
index ca483d0a..02cb6c5d 100644
--- a/HISTORY.md
+++ b/HISTORY.md
@@ -4,6 +4,55 @@ A short, human-readable log of notable changes and the reasoning behind them.
 Newest first. (Detailed, current behaviour lives in `CLAUDE.md`; this file is the
 "why we did it" story.)

+## 2026-07-22 — Course workbooks hosted on the APR site (off Dropbox)
+
+**Why.** Some clients' corporate firewalls block Dropbox but treat
+`agilepainrelief.com` as a normal business site, so attendees couldn't open
+their workbooks (this surfaced right before a CSPO cohort). The content is
+low-sensitivity reference material, so a real auth gate was overkill.
+
+**What we did.**
+- **Serve workbooks as static PDFs under `public/materials/`**, guarded by an
+  unguessable per-course slug (`<course>-<year>-q<quarter>-<16 hex>`, the hex from
+  `openssl rand -hex 8`) plus `X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow` on `/materials/*`
+  in `netlify.toml`. Deliberately **not** in `robots.txt` (a `Disallow` would stop
+  crawlers fetching the file, so they'd never see the `noindex` — the two are in
+  tension) and not in the sitemap (bare `public/` files never enter it). Rejected a
+  real auth gate as disproportionate; recorded in `docs/adr/0001-...`. Chose a new
+  `/materials/` prefix over reusing `/downloads/` to keep public lead magnets and
+  private client workbooks in separate namespaces.
+- **Added a quarterly-updated variable for the workbook link.** The post-course
+  email carries two separate links: `{{var:training_folder}}` (the per-cohort mural
+  export, still on Dropbox, left alone) and the course workbook (previously a
+  hardcoded Dropbox folder in the template body). The workbook link now resolves via
+  `deriveWorkbookUrl()` (`email-automation/src/course-config.ts`) from
+  `courses/workbook-urls.json[type]` — a single source of truth, updated once per
+  quarter when the slug rotates — with an optional per-cohort `workbookUrl` override.
+  Returns null for courses not yet migrated (their template keeps its hardcoded link).
+- **Wired into all three CSPO emails.** The workbook link is `{{var:workbook_link}}`
+  in `pre-7day-cspo.html`, `pre-2day-cspo.html` (the "Download the Digital Workbook"
+  link — the pre-class, firewall-critical one), and `post-cspo.md`. The old links
+  pointed at Dropbox *folders* holding the workbook plus other artifacts that were
+  "not always up to date"; we deliberately point at just the single, current
+  `CSPO Workbook.pdf` and reworded the "files in this Dropbox folder" prose to suit.
+- **Fail-loud reachability check.** For any email (pre or post) whose template
+  references `{{var:workbook_link}}`, the send (including `--dry-run`) requires a
+  configured URL and `assertWorkbookReachable()` HEADs it, aborting on a non-200 —
+  catching a typo'd slug, an unpushed folder, or a filename mismatch before a student
+  is emailed a dead link. Scoped to APR-hosted `/materials/` URLs. Proves the link is
+  live, not that it's current.
+- **CSM/CSD** still hardcode their Dropbox workbook links; `deriveWorkbookUrl` returns
+  null for them, so nothing breaks. Migrating each: host its PDF under `/materials/`,
+  add a line to `workbook-urls.json`, switch its templates to `{{var:workbook_link}}`.
+- **Fixed a latent substitution bug (post-course markdown path).** `marked` runs
+  before variable substitution and percent-encodes the braces of any `{{var:...}}`
+  that sits in a link URL (`href="%7B%7Bvar:...%7D%7D"`), so the later regex never
+  matched — every URL-position variable shipped unsubstituted. This had silently
+  broken the murals `{{var:training_folder}}` link in every post email (it's only
+  ever a URL), and would have broken the new workbook link too. Fix: in
+  `renderMarkdownEmail`, decode `%7B%7B`/`%7D%7D` back to braces before substituting.
+  The pre-course HTML templates are unaffected (no `marked` step).
+
 ## 2026-07-16 — Astro 6 → 7 upgrade

 **Why.** Staying current with the framework. `npx @astrojs/upgrade` aborted with
diff --git a/email-automation/CLAUDE.md b/email-automation/CLAUDE.md
index 06c6b19e..71cd13fe 100644
--- a/email-automation/CLAUDE.md
+++ b/email-automation/CLAUDE.md
@@ -316,7 +316,21 @@ Optional fields (have defaults):
 - `timezone` — IANA timezone, e.g. `"America/Toronto"` (default)
 - `location` — e.g. `"Virtual"` (default), `"In-Person"`
 - `googleDocsFolder` — only needed for CSM courses
-- `dropboxFolder` — post-course training materials link
+- `dropboxFolder` — the **per-cohort mural export** Dropbox folder (post-course only). Shown in the post email as `{{var:training_folder}}`. This is where Mark exports the class's murals after the cohort; it is per-cohort and unrelated to the workbook.
+- `workbookUrl` — optional per-cohort override for the hosted workbook link. Normally omitted (the link is resolved by course type; see below). Set it only for a one-off cohort that needs a different URL.
+
+### Post-course workbook link
+
+Two different links live in the post-course email, and they are deliberately separate:
+
+- **Mural export** — `{{var:training_folder}}`, from the per-cohort `config.dropboxFolder`. Changes every cohort. Still on Dropbox (out of scope for the workbook move).
+- **Course workbook** — `{{var:workbook_link}}`, the workbook PDF hosted on the APR site. Resolved by `deriveWorkbookUrl(config)` in `src/course-config.ts`: (1) `config.workbookUrl` cohort override, else (2) `courses/workbook-urls.json[type]`, else `null` (course not yet migrated — its template then still hardcodes its own link).
+
+`courses/workbook-urls.json` maps course type → the current direct PDF URL on the APR site (`https://agilepainrelief.com/materials/<course>-<year>-q<quarter>-<hex>/<file>.pdf`). It is the **single place to update once per quarter** when the site's `/materials/` slug rotates. Must be the direct PDF URL (bare files have no folder index) with spaces `%20`-encoded.
+
+`{{var:workbook_link}}` appears in all three CSPO templates — `pre-7day` and `pre-2day` (the "Download the Digital Workbook" link, the pre-class firewall-critical one) and `post` — so migrating a course means switching each of its templates to the variable. (CSM/CSD still hardcode their Dropbox links pending migration.)
+
+When any email's template (pre or post) references `{{var:workbook_link}}`, that send (including `--dry-run`) requires a configured URL and runs `assertWorkbookReachable()`: a `HEAD` (falling back to a ranged `GET`) that **aborts on a non-200**, so a typo'd slug, an unpushed folder, or a filename mismatch can't email students a dead link. The check is scoped to `agilepainrelief.com/materials/` URLs. It proves the link is *live*, not that it's the *current* workbook. Templates that still hardcode a Dropbox link are unaffected until migrated.

 Derived automatically:
 - `dateFormatted` (e.g. "Feb 17-18"), `daysOfWeek` (e.g. "Tuesday-Wednesday") — from `date` + `numberOfDays`
@@ -331,6 +345,7 @@ that are substituted locally in Node before sending raw HTML to Cakemail:
 - `{{var:first_name}}`, `{{var:course_dates}}`, `{{var:class_times}}`, `{{var:meeting_invite}}`
 - `{{var:google_calendar_url}}`, `{{var:outlook_calendar_url}}`
 - `{{var:mural_link}}`, `{{var:zoom_link}}`, `{{var:google_docs_folder}}`
+- `{{var:workbook_link}}` — the hosted course workbook PDF (see "Post-course workbook link"; despite the heading, the same variable is used by the pre-7day / pre-2day templates for the "Download the Digital Workbook" link)

 ### Post-course Markdown Email Templates
 Post-course emails are written in Markdown (`templates/course/post-csm.md`, `post-cspo.md`)
@@ -340,7 +355,8 @@ header/footer shell).

 **Available variables in Markdown templates:**
 - `{{var:first_name}}` — recipient's first name
-- `{{var:training_folder}}` — course-specific Dropbox link (from `config.dropboxFolder`)
+- `{{var:training_folder}}` — the **per-cohort mural export** Dropbox folder (from `config.dropboxFolder`). Mark exports the class's murals here after each cohort. This is NOT the workbook.
+- `{{var:workbook_link}}` — the hosted **course workbook** link, resolved by `deriveWorkbookUrl()` (see "Post-course workbook link" below). Only the templates of migrated courses reference it; when they do, the send is reachability-checked and aborts on a non-200.

 **Wrapper template:**
 - `post-wrapper.html` — the MJML-compiled header/footer shell, contains logo, social
